#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:12
msgid "Abstract"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:14
msgid ""
"This PEP proposes disallowing bare ``except:`` clauses in Python's exception-"
"handling syntax. Currently, Python allows catching all exceptions with a "
"bare ``except:`` clause, which can lead to overly broad exception handling "
"and mask important errors. This PEP suggests requiring explicit exception "
"types in all except clauses, promoting more precise and intentional error "
"handling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:22
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:24
msgid ""
"The current syntax allows for catching all exceptions with a bare ``except:"
"`` clause:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:33
msgid ""
"While this syntax can be convenient for a \"catch all\" handler, it often "
"leads to poor coding practices:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:36
msgid "It can mask important errors that should be propagated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:37
msgid ""
"It makes debugging more difficult by catching and potentially hiding "
"unexpected exceptions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:39
msgid "It goes against the Python principle of explicit over implicit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:41
msgid ""
"Various linters [1]_ [2]_ [3]_ and style guides (including :pep:`8`) [4]_ "
"[5]_ [6]_ [7]_ discourage bare ``except`` clauses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:44
msgid ""
"By requiring explicit exception types, we can encourage more thoughtful and "
"precise error handling:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:54
msgid ""
"Another view of this problem is that bare except handlers are ambiguous "
"regarding the intended handling of terminating exceptions, as the intention "
"could have been either:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:58
msgid ""
"Only catch non-terminating exceptions (``except Exception:``). If this was "
"the intention, using a bare ``except:`` is an outright bug, since that isn't "
"what it means."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:61
msgid ""
"Catch all exceptions, including terminating ones (``except BaseException:"
"``). using bare ``except:`` here it is at least correct, but readers need to "
"check to be sure it isn't an instance of the first case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:65
msgid ""
"Since both possible intentions have available unambiguous spellings, the "
"ambiguous form is redundant and that's why we propose to disallow it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:69
msgid "Rationale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:71
msgid ""
"The decision to disallow bare except clauses is based on the following "
"considerations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:74
msgid ""
"Requiring specific exception types makes the programmer's intentions clear "
"and encourages thinking about what exceptions might occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:77
msgid ""
"Catching only specific exceptions makes identifying and debugging unexpected "
"errors easier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:80
msgid ""
"Preventing overly broad exception handling reduces the risk of silently "
"ignoring critical errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:83
msgid ""
"Many style guides and linters already discourage the use of bare except "
"clauses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:88
msgid "Specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:90
msgid ""
"The syntax for the except clause will be modified to require an exception "
"type. The grammar will be updated to remove the possibility of adding an "
"empty expression in except clauses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:94
msgid ""
"This change disallows the bare ``except:`` syntax. All except clauses must "
"specify at least one exception type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:108
msgid ""
"The semantics of exception handling remain unchanged, except that it will no "
"longer be possible to catch all exceptions without explicitly specifying "
"``BaseException`` or a similarly broad exception type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:114
msgid "Backwards Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:116
msgid ""
"This change is not backwards compatible. Existing code that uses bare "
"``except:`` clauses will need to be modified. To ease the transition:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:119
msgid ""
"A deprecation warning will be issued for bare except clauses in Python 3.14."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:120
msgid "The syntax will be fully disallowed in Python 3.17."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:121
msgid ""
"A ``from __future__ import strict_excepts`` will be provided to invalidate "
"bare except handlers in earlier versions of Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:124
msgid ""
"A tool will be provided to automatically update code to replace bare "
"``except:`` with ``except BaseException:``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:129
msgid "Security Implications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:131
msgid "This change has no security implications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:135
msgid "How to Teach This"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:137
msgid ""
"For new Python users, exception handling should be taught with explicit "
"exception types from the start:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:151
msgid ""
"For experienced users, the change can be introduced as a best practice that "
"is now enforced by the language. The following points should be emphasized:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:154
msgid "Always catch specific exceptions when possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:155
msgid "Use ``except Exception:`` as a last resort for truly unexpected errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:156
msgid "Never silence exceptions without careful consideration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:158
msgid ""
"Documentation should guide common exception hierarchies and how to choose "
"appropriate exception types to catch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:162
msgid "Rejected ideas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:164
msgid ""
"There are genuine cases where the use of bare ``except:`` handlers are "
"correct. one of the examples that have been raised from Mailman [8]_ "
"involves handling transactions in the face of any exception:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:181
msgid ""
"This code guarantees that no matter what exception occurs, any open "
"transaction will be aborted, while in the successful condition, the "
"transaction will be committed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0760.rst:185
msgid ""
"We do believe that although there are cases such like this one where bare "
"``except:`` handlers are correct, it would be better to actually be explicit "
"and use ``except BaseException:`` for the reasons indicated in the "
"\"Motivation\" section."
msgstr ""

